---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import pulse from "../assets/pulse-001.png";
import Disclosure from "../components/Disclosure.astro";
import Question from "../components/Question.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const DOWNLOAD_URL =
	"https://github.com/summerhammer/yellowhammer/releases/latest/download/Yellowhammer.dmg";
const REPO_URL = "https://github.com/summerhammer/yellowhammer";

const primaryButton =
	"btn inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-primary px-5 py-2.5 text-base font-semibold text-on-primary hover:bg-primary-hover";
const secondaryButton =
	"btn inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-outline px-5 py-2 text-base font-semibold text-ink hover:bg-tint";
const link = "font-medium text-link underline underline-offset-4 decoration-2";

const questions = [
	["what-is-it", "What is it?"],
	["never-does", "What does it never do?"],
	["agent-fails", "What happens when an agent fails?"],
	["what-you-need", "What do I need?"],
	["touch-main", "Does it touch main?"],
	["open-source", "Is it open source?"],
	["start", "How do I start?"],
];

const needs = [
	"A Mac on macOS 26.",
	"Orca ADE, which creates and cleans up the Worktrees.",
	"A Linear workspace, which holds the board.",
	"GitHub, where the pull requests open.",
	"At least one supported agent CLI, which does the coding.",
];
---

<Layout
	title="Yellowhammer: questions and answers"
	description="Yellowhammer runs an unattended Night per Project on a Mac. It never writes a line of code and never merges to main."
>
	<a
		href="#main"
		class="sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:left-4 focus:top-4 focus:rounded-lg focus:bg-card focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:text-ink"
		>Skip to content</a
	>

	<header class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-3 px-4 py-5 sm:px-6">
		<a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-lg" aria-label="Yellowhammer, home">
			<img src="/yellowhammer-mark.svg" alt="" width="1024" height="1024" class="size-10" />
			<span class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Yellowhammer</span>
		</a>
		<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1">
			<a href={DOWNLOAD_URL} class={primaryButton}>
				<svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 3v10m0 0-4-4m4 4 4-4M4 17h12"></path></svg>
				Download for Mac
			</a>
			<span class="text-sm text-muted">Requires macOS 26</span>
		</div>
	</header>

	<main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-16 sm:px-6">
		<div class="relative isolate py-10 sm:py-14">
			<div class="sun absolute -top-6 right-0 -z-10 size-64 sm:size-80" aria-hidden="true"></div>
			<img
				src="/yellowhammer-mark.svg"
				alt="Yellowhammer mark"
				width="1024"
				height="1024"
				class="size-20 sm:size-24"
			/>
			<h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl">
				Yellowhammer runs an unattended Night on your repositories.
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-5 max-w-[60ch] text-xl leading-relaxed text-muted">
				One Night per Project, on top of Orca ADE. You read the result in the morning.
			</p>
			<nav aria-labelledby="questions-heading" class="mt-8">
				<h2 id="questions-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">
					Seven questions
				</h2>
				<ol class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
					{
						questions.map(([id, label]) => (
							<li>
								<a
									href={`#${id}`}
									class="btn inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-full border border-line bg-card px-4 py-2 text-base font-medium text-link hover:bg-tint"
								>
									{label}
								</a>
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ol>
			</nav>
		</div>

		<div class="space-y-6">
			<Question id="what-is-it" question="What is it?">
				<p>
					Yellowhammer is a Mac app that runs an unattended Night for each of your Projects. It takes
					intent from a Linear board. When the board is empty, it authors the work itself from your
					specification.
				</p>
				<p>
					Each Work Card goes to an agent CLI and runs in its own Worktree. The Night ends with one
					pull request per repository. You read the result in the morning.
				</p>
				<Disclosure summary="What happens in a Night?">
					<ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 marker:font-semibold">
						<li>It takes intent from a Linear board, or authors the work when the board is empty.</li>
						<li>It writes a Definition of Done for each Work Card before any code exists.</li>
						<li>It routes each Work Card to an agent CLI.</li>
						<li>It runs the Work Cards of each repository in order, in one Worktree: a Repo Lane.</li>
						<li>It opens one pull request per repository.</li>
						<li>It verifies the result against the Definition of Done.</li>
						<li>It reports back to the board in a Night Summary.</li>
					</ol>
				</Disclosure>
				<figure class="pt-2">
					<Image
						src={pulse}
						alt="The Yellowhammer Pulse window after a Night. The tiles read: Needs you 0, Now idle, Feature 3 of 3 Cards, Night done, Health OK. The inspector shows one pull request, number 471, and three Work Cards marked Done."
						width={1280}
						widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
						sizes="(min-width: 768px) 672px, calc(100vw - 4rem)"
						format="webp"
						loading="lazy"
						class="h-auto w-full rounded-xl"
					/>
					<figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">
						The Pulse, the app's status view, after a Night. Nothing needs you.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</Question>

			<Question id="never-does" question="What does it never do?">
				<p>
					<strong>It never writes a line of code, and it never merges to main.</strong>
					The agent CLIs write the code. Yellowhammer judges between them.
				</p>
				<p>It hands off at the pull request. The merge is yours.</p>
				<Disclosure summary="Also out of scope">
					<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
						<li>Deploy and release. Never, not deferred.</li>
						<li>
							Cloud execution. Your code, credentials and models stay on your machine, and the Night
							rides the subscriptions you already have.
						</li>
						<li>A second board. Linear is the board.</li>
					</ul>
				</Disclosure>
			</Question>

			<Question id="agent-fails" question="What happens when an agent fails?">
				<p>The work stops, and the board says why. Yellowhammer does not grind.</p>
				<p>
					Bounds limit the work, and you set them per Project. When a Bound fires,
					it stops work and carries the reason, or it promotes the item to a standing decision. A retry
					never lands on a route that already failed.
				</p>
				<div class="space-y-3">
					<Disclosure summary="Bounds">
						<p>
							A Bound is a numeric limit you set. Each one is reported in the Night Summary, so you
							see how close the Night came.
						</p>
						<p>
							Review rounds end an Attempt, and the next Attempt runs on a different route. Attempts
							per Work Card Block the Work Card once they are spent.
						</p>
					</Disclosure>
					<Disclosure summary="Blocks">
						<p>
							A Blocked Work Card does not move until a human acts. It carries a Block Reason, so you
							know where to look without opening anything.
						</p>
						<p>The reasons include reviewer rejection, check failure, route failure and reply overdue.</p>
					</Disclosure>
					<Disclosure summary="Waiting on You">
						<p>
							Waiting on You is a Linear workflow state. The Work Card is assigned to you, and the
							question is in a comment. Answer it in Linear, not in the app.
						</p>
						<p>
							A Work Card lands there when an agent asks instead of guessing, when it no longer fits
							the repositories as they stand, or when it would touch a Protected Path. If you stay
							silent for the number of Nights you set, it becomes Blocked.
						</p>
					</Disclosure>
				</div>
			</Question>

			<Question id="what-you-need" question="What do I need?">
				<p>Five things. It runs on your Mac and uses the tools you already have.</p>
				<ul class="space-y-2">
					{
						needs.map((item) => (
							<li class="flex gap-3">
								<span class="mt-2.5 size-2 flex-none rounded-full bg-info" aria-hidden="true" />
								<span>{item}</span>
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ul>
			</Question>

			<Question id="touch-main" question="Does it touch main?">
				<p>No. It never merges to main.</p>
				<p>
					Each repository gets one Feature Branch, built in its own Worktree. Yellowhammer pushes the
					branch and opens one pull request. You review it and merge it.
				</p>
			</Question>

			<Question id="open-source" question="Is it open source?">
				<p>Yes. Yellowhammer is open source under the MIT licence.</p>
				<p>
					<a href={REPO_URL} class={link}>Read the source on GitHub</a>.
				</p>
			</Question>

			<Question id="start" question="How do I start?">
				<p>Download the app for your Mac. Check the list under "What do I need?" first.</p>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-3 pt-1">
					<a href={DOWNLOAD_URL} class={primaryButton}>
						<svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 3v10m0 0-4-4m4 4 4-4M4 17h12"></path></svg>
						Download for Mac
					</a>
					<a href={REPO_URL} class={secondaryButton}>Star on GitHub</a>
				</div>
				<p class="text-base text-muted">Requires macOS 26.</p>
			</Question>
		</div>
	</main>

	<footer class="border-t border-line">
		<div class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-3 px-4 py-8 text-sm text-muted sm:px-6">
			<p>&copy; Summer Hammer, LLC</p>
			<p>
				MIT licence.
				<a href={REPO_URL} class={link}>Source on GitHub</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</footer>
</Layout>
